  "body": "## Finding description \n\nProtocol : Launchpad \n\nThe Launchpad system is designed to launch several new tokens/pairs,\nand so it has an `updateLaunchpadLPVault()` function to flexibly modify its LP vaults.\nEvery time a new pair is graduated, the LP tokens are minted to the latest modified LP vault,   \nwhile adding initial liquidity. [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/main/contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol#L500-L509)\n\n```solidity\n        uniV2Router.addLiquidity({\n            tokenA: token,\n            tokenB: address(data.quote),\n            amountADesired: tokensToLock,\n            amountBDesired: quoteToLock,\n            amountAMin: 0,\n            amountBMin: 0,\n            to: address(launchpadLPVault),    // <@ updated new vault\n            deadline: block.timestamp\n        });\n```\n\nHowever it has an architectural issue.    \nThe `LaunchpadLPVault` address is immutable in the Factory contract. \nEvery time a new pair is created from the Factory , the pairs are initialized with the original `_launchpadLp`address.\n\n```solidity\n// FACTORY: Immutable vault address\nconstructor(..., address _launchpadLp, ...) {\n    launchpadLp = _launchpadLp; // Set once, NOT changeable\n}\nIUniswapV2Pair(pair).initialize(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, // // <@ Still uses old LPvault\n              _launchpadFeeDistributor);  \n\n// PAIR: Immutable vault address per pair\nfunction initialize(..., address _launchpadLp, ...) {          \n    launchpadLp = _launchpadLp; // Set once per pair, NOT changeable\n}\n\n```\n\n\nSo every time a swap is made while rewards are active, the `_getLaunchpadFees` function uses the original LPvault `launchpadLp` which has 0 LP tokens. \n\n```solidity\n    function _getLaunchpadFees(uint256 amount0In, uint256 amount1In)\n        internal view returns (uint112 fee0, uint112 fee1)\n    {\n\n        uint256 totalLpBal = this.totalSupply();\n        uint256 launchpadLpBal = this.balanceOf(launchpadLp) + MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY;\n\n        if (amount0In > 0) fee0 = uint112(amount0In.mul(REWARDS_FEE_SHARE).mul(launchpadLpBal) / (totalLpBal * 1000));\n        if (amount1In > 0) fee1 = uint112(amount1In.mul(REWARDS_FEE_SHARE).mul(launchpadLpBal) / (totalLpBal * 1000));\n\n        return (fee0, fee1);\n    }\n\n```\n\nIn Summary, the LP tokens are sent to the new vault, while new Pairs continue using the old LPvault's address for fee calculations. This completely breaks the fee calculation / distribution mechanism.\n\nThe calculated fees (dust amounts or 0) are either extremely lower than the expected fees, or 0 for most cases.\n\n## Vulnerable Path\n\n1. Factory deployed with immutable LPvault1\n2. Pairs created → all use LPvault1 for fee calculations\n3. Launchpad updates to LPvault2\n4. New LP tokens minted to LPvault2\n5. But further new pairs are still initialized with LPvault1\n6. Pairs still check LPvault1's balance for fee calculations →  returns 0\n7. REWARD SYSTEM BROKEN\n\n## Impact and Likelihood\n\n\nImpact : High\n\n1. `GTELaunchpadV2Pair`'s Fee calculations are completely broken.\n2. No Reward fees are distributed to users.\n3. Sell pressure on the token as users don't get rewards from holding.\n\nLikelihood : Medium\n1. All newly graduated pairs are affected after an LPvault update\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAdd a function in the `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory ` to update the `launchpadLp` address, \nwhenever it is updated in the LaunchPad.",
  "proof_of_concept": "A foundry POC showing, the actual fees calculated are much lower than expected fees.\nActual calculated fees are almost  0 for most cases.\n\n```solidity\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\n\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport {LaunchpadLPVault} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchpadLPVault.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is LaunchpadTestBase {\n\n\n    function test_LaunchpadLPVault_AddressUpdateBreaksFees() external {\n        console.log(\"=== CRITICAL: Vault Address Update Breaks Fee Calculations ===\\n\");\n        \n        // Setup: Create factory with initial vault\n        LaunchpadLPVault vault1 = launchpadLPVault; // Initial vault\n        \n        GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory realFactory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(\n            address(this),\n            address(launchpad),\n            address(vault1),      // Initial vault address\n            address(distributor)\n        );\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n 1. === Initial Setup ===\");\n        console.log(\"Vault1 address:\", address(vault1));\n        console.log(\"Factory's immutable launchpadLp:\", address(vault1));\n \n        // Create and deploy new vault2\n        LaunchpadLPVault vault2 = new LaunchpadLPVault();\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n 2. === Updating to New Vault ===\");\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        // Update launchpad to use vault2 (but factory still uses vault1!)\n        launchpad.updateLaunchpadLPVault(address(vault2));\n        address LaunchPad_LPAddy = address(launchpad.launchpadLPVault());\n        console.log(\"\\n===LP Vault updated. Launchpad LPvault new address : \", LaunchPad_LPAddy );\n\n\n        // Note: Factory's launchpadLp is IMMUTABLE and still points to vault1\n        \n        // Create new  pair - it will STILL use vault1 because factory is immutable!\n        ERC20Harness tokenC = new ERC20Harness(\"TokenC\", \"TKC\");\n        ERC20Harness tokenD = new ERC20Harness(\"TokenD\", \"TKD\");\n        \n        vm.prank(address(launchpad));\n        address pair2Address = realFactory.createPair(address(tokenC), address(tokenD));\n        GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair2 = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(pair2Address);\n\n        // Simulate: LP tokens for pair2 go to vault2 (new vault) during addLiquidity\n        tokenC.mint(address(this), 100e18);\n        tokenD.mint(address(this), 100e18);\n        tokenC.transfer(pair2Address, 100e18);\n        tokenD.transfer(pair2Address, 100e18);\n        pair2.mint(address(vault2)); // LP tokens to NEW vault2\n\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n 3.===  Pair2 Created After Vault Update ===\");\n        console.log(\"Pair2's launchpadLp (still vault1!):\", pair2.launchpadLp());\n        assertTrue(pair2.launchpadLp() == address(vault1), \"Pair2 still uses vault1!\");\n        \n        // But new liquidity would go to vault2 (if launchpad.addLiquidity uses updated address)\n   \n        uint256 vault2LPBalance = pair2.balanceOf(address(vault2));\n        uint256 vault1Pair2Balance = pair2.balanceOf(address(vault1));\n        \n        console.log(\"\\nPair2 LP token distribution:\");\n        console.log(\"LP tokens in vault2 (actual location):\", vault2LPBalance);\n        console.log(\"LP tokens in vault1 (where pair checks):\", vault1Pair2Balance);\n            \n        // In _getLaunchpadFees(), pair2 checks vault1 balance (which is 0!)\n        uint256 totalSupply = pair2.totalSupply();\n        uint256 launchpadLpBal = pair2.balanceOf(pair2.launchpadLp()) + 1000; // MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY\n        \n        console.log(\"Total LP supply:\", totalSupply);\n        console.log(\"Launchpad LP balance (checking wrong vault!):\", launchpadLpBal, \"(MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY)\");\n        console.log(\"Actual LP balance in correct vault:\", vault2LPBalance);\n\n\n        // Calculate fees using pair's perspective\n        console.log(\"\\n 4. === Fee Calculation Breakdown Example swap Using 10 WETH===\");\n        // Fee calculation will be WRONG\n        uint256 swapAmount = 10e18; // 10 WETH\n        uint256 REWARDS_FEE_SHARE = 1; // 0.1% fee to rewards\n        uint256 expectedCorrectFee = (swapAmount * REWARDS_FEE_SHARE * vault2LPBalance) / (totalSupply * 1000);\n        uint256 actualWrongFee = (swapAmount * REWARDS_FEE_SHARE * launchpadLpBal) / (totalSupply * 1000);\n\n        console.log(\"Expected CORRECT fee (using correct balance):\", expectedCorrectFee);\n        console.log(\"Actual WRONG  fee (using wrong vault):\", actualWrongFee);\n        console.log(\"Fee calculation is BROKEN!\");\n        \n        assertTrue(actualWrongFee < expectedCorrectFee, \"Fee calculation is wrong\");\n        \n    }\n}\n\n```",
